        "terminal": {
          "text": "I chose **the bring-up fixture** and recorded why in [concepts.md](/var/tmp/storyfolio-entry-runtime-20261012/storyfolio-evals/build-full-journey-1-vfhAO9/docs/story/concepts.md): you built it, and it makes the connection between firmware, bench access and physical observation tangible.\n\nThe [full storyboard](/var/tmp/storyfolio-entry-runtime-20261012/storyfolio-evals/build-full-journey-1-vfhAO9/docs/story/storyboard.md) follows a bench checklist:\n\n| Chapter | What it establishes |\n|---|---|\n| Purpose | Your name, contribution and central question |\n| Setup | Your firmware/fixture work and your colleague’s hardware responsibility |\n| Exercise | Working documents and the labelled teaching cycle |\n| Observe | The radio-awake observation, with its unresolved limits |\n| Record limits | Projection versus run, samples versus deployment, preliminary check versus qualification |\n| Handover | The answer: connect decisions to observations, then keep claims within their evidence |\n\nThe same six solid fixture modules carry the whole story. I propose **10 beats across 12 screen heights**—enough for this single project without repeating claims.\n\nI also planned:\n\n- A standalone Mosslink project page.\n- A readable, printable CV and self-contained HTML download.\n- Email, ordinary site navigation and chapter links.\n- Local share-preview artwork, an icon and a useful missing-page page.\n- Complete HTML content and static explanations when 3D or JavaScript is unavailable.\n\nI selected system fonts and proposed three appearance studies for your later choice. Everything remains local, using the available tools.\n\n**Approve this storyboard, including the shorter 10-beat structure, or tell me what to change.**\n\nThe [storyfolio skill](/var/tmp/storyfolio-entry-runtime-20261012/storyfolio-evals/build-full-journey-1-vfhAO9/.agents/skills/storyfolio/SKILL.md) requires storyboard approval before building the chosen site: “They have said yes to it.” Once approved, I’ll build the opening, observation and ending for you to compare the three looks.",
